;;; sha256sum_dispatch_x86.shard — THE DISPATCH BIN's machine article
;;; (Arc B rung B6, slice C — docs/STREAM.md 9.2/9.3). One module, both
;;; landed variants, a proven CPUID choice between them: the R2 plain-name
;;; artifact `sha256sum`.
;;;
;;; THE MERGED MODULE (spelled by R3's linking composition in every claim):
;;;   (MkXModule (xlk_app SCALAR15 (xlk_app (xlk_shfns 15 SHANI15)
;;;                                         (Cons DISPATCH-MAIN Nil)))
;;;              65536 131072)
;;; SCALAR15 = the B3 streaming skeleton's fifteen functions verbatim at
;;; indices 0-14 (transfers by EXTENSION, entry 9); SHANI15 = the B5
;;; variant's fifteen, shifted to 15-29 by xlk_shfns (transfers by SHIFT,
;;; entry 24 = 9+15); the dispatch main is fn 30, the bin entry.
;;;
;;; THE STUB (R4's two-step, fn 30): CPUID leaf 0 from the all-zero file
;;; (draws eax/ebx/ecx/edx from lxans — R1, no trace event); if max basic
;;; leaf < 7, scalar. Else CPUID leaf 7 subleaf 0, test EBX bit 29 (SHA):
;;; clear -> scalar, set -> SHA-NI. Every taken path re-zeroes the four
;;; clobbered registers before XCall — both variant towers enter from the
;;; all-zero register file. Pre-2013 silicon answers out-of-range leaves
;;; with the highest basic leaf's data, which is why the leaf-0 gate must
;;; precede the bit test (STREAM.md 9.1 R4).
;;;
;;; THE PROOF LADDER, bottom to top:
;;;  - sdb_*/vdb_*: the six landed variant entry verdicts restated at BODY
;;;    grain (weval_seq / wveval_seq over the ORIGINAL variant modules) —
;;;    minus-one-unfold replays of ssm_main_*/ssw_main_eof and
;;;    vsm_main_*/vsw_main_eof; the run wrapper maps WExit to itself and
;;;    None to None, so every RHS carries over verbatim. The ratified
;;;    exit-propagation call lemma DISSOLVED into plain evaluation here:
;;;    with body-grain facts the call arm just computes, and the dry leg
;;;    (None, which does not invert through the wrapper) needs no special
;;;    treatment (the slice-B seam item, decided as ratified).
;;;  - sdw_*: the scalar body facts crossed world -> world-vector by
;;;    xlk_embw at (XQS body) with ANY entry XMM file (None rides; the
;;;    semantic-ok premise computes on the delivered value).
;;;  - sdt_*/vdt_*: both families transferred onto the merged module —
;;;    xlk_extwv for the unshifted scalar family, xlk_shwv (via the
;;;    query shift xlk_shq) for the shifted SHA-NI family. Every linking
;;;    premise (module ctor equations, call-resolution cbq/cbfns, d =
;;;    xlk_len pre) is refl-grade or computes on the ground lists.
;;;  - dsm_main_{eof,err,dry}_{lo,hi}: THE D8 DISJUNCTION at the bin
;;;    boundary xvrun_w, fn 30, all-zero registers, QUANTIFIED XMM file,
;;;    chip answers as quantified oracle draws ahead of the variant
;;;    answer list. _lo = 4 draws, premise maxleaf < 7 (old silicon):
;;;    the scalar family always runs. _hi = 8 draws, premise maxleaf >=
;;;    7: the proof case-splits on EBX bit 29 of the second draw-set and
;;;    cites the matching family's transferred verdict — BOTH branches
;;;    deliver the SAME canonical RHS (eof: WVExit 0 with LxWrote
;;;    (bytes_hex (sha256 (scat (ssw_chunks its)))); err: WVExit 1 after
;;;    LxReadErr; dry: None on answer exhaustion). Chip-short answer
;;;    lists refuse through wcpuid exactly like mid-read exhaustion
;;;    refuses through lx_step — the lx convention covers both, as B3's
;;;    D8 closure ruled.
;;;
;;; FUEL: N = 1610 calibrated. Scalar legs reach their call with the body
;;; walk at exactly S^1601 (ssm_fuel its f) — the verdicts' own spelling.
;;; The SHA-NI leg sits 8 units deeper (body at S^1593) and its verdict
;;; wants S^1390: the slack rides through f via the local transparent pad
;;; (dsm_pad, with dsm_fuel_pad commuting it through ssm_fuel; std/nat's
;;; add_nat is opaque by module discipline, hence the local pad).
;;;
;;; Landed from b6c1/b6c2/b6c4 root probes, 2026-08-10.

